WEBVTT

00:00:10.494 --> 00:00:13.193
You're sure Katie did not
have this in her possession

00:00:13.236 --> 00:00:16.326
when she entered
the Three Broomsticks?

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:18.415
It's like I said.

00:00:18.459 --> 00:00:20.417
She left to go to the loo,

00:00:20.461 --> 00:00:23.203
and when she came back
she had the package.

00:00:24.465 --> 00:00:27.076
She said it was important
that she deliver it.

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:29.513
Did she say to whom?

00:00:29.557 --> 00:00:31.646
To Professor Dumbledore.

00:00:31.689 --> 00:00:34.649
Very well. Thank you, Leanne.
You may go.

00:00:39.872 --> 00:00:44.746
Why is it when something happens
it is always you three?

00:00:45.747 --> 00:00:47.270
Believe me, professor,

00:00:47.314 --> 00:00:50.578
I've been asking myself
the same question for six years.

00:00:50.621 --> 00:00:52.319
Oh, Severus.

00:00:55.235 --> 00:00:57.890
[SHRIEKING, CLAMORING]

00:00:57.933 --> 00:00:59.892
What do you think?

00:01:01.719 --> 00:01:06.594
I think Miss Bell
is lucky to be alive.

00:01:06.637 --> 00:01:09.553
She was cursed, wasn't she?
I know Katie,

00:01:09.597 --> 00:01:11.904
off the Quidditch pitch,
she wouldn't hurt a fly.

00:01:11.947 --> 00:01:14.167
If she was delivering that
to Professor Dumbledore,

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:15.951
she wasn't doing it knowingly.

00:01:15.995 --> 00:01:18.040
Yes, she was cursed.

00:01:18.084 --> 00:01:20.521
It was Malfoy.

00:01:23.045 --> 00:01:26.222
That is a very serious
accusation, Potter.

00:01:26.266 --> 00:01:28.572
Indeed.

00:01:28.616 --> 00:01:29.791
Your evidence?

00:01:29.834 --> 00:01:32.098
I just know.

00:01:32.141 --> 00:01:34.274
You just...

00:01:36.015 --> 00:01:37.712
know.

00:01:40.454 --> 00:01:42.456
You astonish with your gifts,
Potter.

00:01:42.499 --> 00:01:46.547
Gifts mere mortals
can only dream of possessing.

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:51.944
How grand it must be
to be the Chosen One.

00:01:57.471 --> 00:01:59.777
I suggest you go back
to your dormitories.

00:01:59.821 --> 00:02:01.083
All of you.

00:02:12.094 --> 00:02:14.531
RON:
What do you suppose Dean
sees in her? Ginny?

00:02:16.098 --> 00:02:18.231
Well, what does she see in him?

00:02:18.274 --> 00:02:20.624
Dean? He's brilliant.

00:02:20.668 --> 00:02:23.627
You called him a slick git
not five hours ago.

00:02:23.671 --> 00:02:25.586
Yeah, well,
he was running his hands

00:02:25.629 --> 00:02:27.588
all over my sister,
wasn't he?

00:02:27.631 --> 00:02:31.157
Something snaps, and you've
gotta hate him, you know?

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:32.288
On principle.

00:02:32.332 --> 00:02:34.464
I suppose.

00:02:35.726 --> 00:02:39.469
So, what is it he sees in her?I don't know.

00:02:39.513 --> 00:02:42.037
She's smart, funny.

00:02:42.081 --> 00:02:45.084
Attractive.Attractive?

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:49.871
You know, she's got nice skin.Skin?

00:02:49.914 --> 00:02:51.960
You're saying Dean's
dating my sister

00:02:52.004 --> 00:02:53.614
because of her skin?Well, no, I mean,

00:02:53.657 --> 00:02:57.574
I'm just-- I'm saying it could
be a contributing factor.

00:03:00.751 --> 00:03:02.579
Hermione's got nice skin.

00:03:02.623 --> 00:03:06.366
Wouldn't you say?
As skin goes, I mean.

00:03:06.409 --> 00:03:09.108
I've never really
thought about it...

00:03:10.544 --> 00:03:12.981
but, I suppose, yeah.

00:03:13.025 --> 00:03:14.591
Very nice.

00:03:18.856 --> 00:03:20.423
I think I'll be going
to sleep now.

00:03:20.467 --> 00:03:22.382
Right. Yeah.

00:03:31.913 --> 00:03:33.219
SLUGHORN:
So tell me, Cormac,

00:03:33.262 --> 00:03:34.350
do you see anything of your

00:03:34.394 --> 00:03:36.178
Uncle Tiberius these days?

00:03:36.222 --> 00:03:38.876
CORMAC:
Yes, sir. In fact,
I'm meant to go hunting with him

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:41.227
and the Minister of Magic
over the holidays.

00:03:41.270 --> 00:03:44.360
Well, be sure to give
them both my best.

00:03:44.404 --> 00:03:45.796
What about your uncle, Belby?

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:47.972
For those who don't know,

00:03:48.016 --> 00:03:50.149
Marcus' uncle invented
the Wolfsbane Potion.

00:03:50.192 --> 00:03:52.977
Is he working on anything new?Don't know.

00:03:53.021 --> 00:03:54.414
Him and Dad don't get on.

00:03:54.457 --> 00:03:56.720
Probably because me dad
says potions are rubbish.

00:03:56.764 --> 00:03:58.896
Says the only potion
worth having

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:00.376
is a stiff one
at the end of the day.

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:02.117
What about you, Miss Granger?

00:04:02.161 --> 00:04:04.163
What exactly does your family
do in the Muggle world?

00:04:06.774 --> 00:04:08.776
My parents are dentists.

00:04:13.172 --> 00:04:14.564
They tend to people's teeth.

00:04:14.608 --> 00:04:16.871
Fascinating.

00:04:16.914 --> 00:04:19.395
And is that considered
a dangerous profession?

00:04:19.439 --> 00:04:20.440
No.

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:25.706
Although, one boy,
Robbie Fenwick,

00:04:25.749 --> 00:04:27.403
did bite my father once.

00:04:27.447 --> 00:04:28.883
He needed 10 stitches.

00:04:31.494 --> 00:04:33.583
[DOOR OPENS]

00:04:35.716 --> 00:04:38.806
Ah. Miss Weasley.
Come in, come in.

00:04:38.849 --> 00:04:40.590
[DOOR SHUTS]

00:04:40.634 --> 00:04:42.592
HERMIONE [WHISPERING]:
Look at her eyes.

00:04:42.636 --> 00:04:43.854
They've been fighting again,

00:04:43.898 --> 00:04:46.509
her and Dean.

00:04:46.553 --> 00:04:48.294
Sorry. I'm not usually late.

00:04:52.254 --> 00:04:55.127
No matter.
You're just in time for dessert,

00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:56.954
that is, if Belby's
left you any.

00:04:56.998 --> 00:04:58.913
[LAUGHS]

00:05:04.745 --> 00:05:05.920
HARRY:
What?

00:05:05.963 --> 00:05:07.748
Nothing.

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:16.626
SLUGHORN:
Goodbye. Bye-bye.

00:05:22.458 --> 00:05:23.459
Potter.

00:05:23.503 --> 00:05:24.721
I'm sorry, sir.

00:05:24.765 --> 00:05:27.115
I was just admiring
your hourglass.

00:05:28.334 --> 00:05:30.292
Ah, yes.

00:05:30.336 --> 00:05:33.034
A most intriguing object.

00:05:33.077 --> 00:05:34.688
The sand runs in accordance

00:05:34.731 --> 00:05:37.560
with the quality
of the conversation.

00:05:37.604 --> 00:05:41.303
If it is stimulating,
the sand runs slowly.

00:05:41.347 --> 00:05:44.176
If it is not...I think I'll be going then.

00:05:44.219 --> 00:05:46.917
Nonsense. You have nothing
to fear, dear boy.

00:05:46.961 --> 00:05:48.789
As to some of your classmates,

00:05:48.832 --> 00:05:52.923
well, let's just say they're
unlikely to make the shelf.

00:05:52.967 --> 00:05:55.012
The shelf, sir?

00:05:55.056 --> 00:05:57.711
Anyone who aspires to be anyone
hopes to end up here.

00:05:57.754 --> 00:06:02.977
But then again, you already
are someone, aren't you, Harry?

00:06:04.239 --> 00:06:06.328
Did Voldemort ever
make the shelf, sir?

00:06:08.374 --> 00:06:10.985
You knew him, didn't you,
sir, Tom Riddle?

00:06:11.028 --> 00:06:12.987
You were his teacher.

00:06:13.030 --> 00:06:15.032
Mr. Riddle had
a number of teachers

00:06:15.076 --> 00:06:17.034
whilst here at Hogwarts.

00:06:17.078 --> 00:06:18.775
What was he like?

00:06:22.344 --> 00:06:25.347
I'm sorry, sir.
Forgive me.

00:06:25.391 --> 00:06:27.349
He killed my parents.

00:06:30.004 --> 00:06:31.614
Of course.

00:06:31.658 --> 00:06:34.791
It's only natural you
should want to know more,

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:39.318
but I'm afraid I must
disappoint you, Harry.

00:06:39.361 --> 00:06:41.058
When I first met

00:06:41.102 --> 00:06:42.886
young Mr. Riddle,
he was a quiet,

00:06:42.930 --> 00:06:47.282
albeit brilliant, boy committed
to becoming a first-rate wizard.

00:06:47.326 --> 00:06:49.241
Not unlike others I've known.

00:06:49.284 --> 00:06:52.026
Not unlike yourself, in fact.

00:06:53.114 --> 00:06:55.682
If the monster existed

00:06:55.725 --> 00:06:58.902
it was buried deep within.

